and again the norm of $A_{\xi}^{(2)}$ is under control. 




Now we estimate $A_{n,\xi}^{(1)}-A_{\xi}^{(1)}=B_{n,\xi}^{(1)}+B_{n,\xi}^{(2)}$, with
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
     B_{n,\xi}^{(1)}:=\sum_{j\in\mathbb Z}\mathcal  A_{j}^0(\widetilde{{\boldsymbol{\varphi}}}^k)\left(\mathbb E_{\widetilde{\boldsymbol{\varphi}}^k}[e^{-\frac{{\mathrm{i}} Q}{4\pi}\int_{\Sigma_n}^{\mathrm{reg}}K_{n}X_{n}^{k,j}\,{\mathrm{d}} v_n-\mu\int_{\Sigma^{\xi}}M_\beta(X_{n}^{k,j},{\mathrm{d}} v_n)}]
    -\mathbb E_{\widetilde{\boldsymbol{\varphi}}^k}[e^{-\frac{{\mathrm{i}} Q}{4\pi}\int_{\Sigma}^{\mathrm{reg}}KX^{k,j}\,{\mathrm{d}} v-\mu\int_{\Sigma^{\xi}}M_\beta(X^{k,j},{\mathrm{d}} v)}]\right),
