The study of $\langle  T_{s,t,\delta}^+(\theta')F,T_{s,t,\delta}^+(\theta)G \rangle_{L^2}$ again boils down to the estimate of Green's function on a thin annulus. Specifically, denote by $(2\pi)^{-1}G_{D,s+t}$ the Dirichlet Green's function on the annulus $e^{-s-t}\leq|z|\leq e^{s+t}$. Then we have the mixed Green's function $(2\pi)^{-1}G_{D,s+t}^+(z,w):=(2\pi)^{-1}(G_{D,s+t}(z,w)+G_{D,s+t}(z,\bar{w}))$ on the half annulus $e^{-s-t}\leq|z|\leq e^{s+t},\operatorname{Im} z\geq0$. Following the proof of \cref{V_v_estimate}, we need to provide a $\delta$-uniform bound in terms of $s,t,\theta,\theta'$
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
